[metadata]
Name:Rules pilot 431 - Attack first, then Relentless Assault
Goal:Win
Turns:1
Difficulty:Medium
Description:It is your first main phase. You control Hill Giant (3/3) and four untapped Mountains, and have Relentless Assault (untap all creatures that attacked this turn; after this main phase there is an additional combat phase followed by an additional main phase) in hand. The opponent is at 6 life and controls no creatures. Reduce the opponent to 0 life this turn.
Rule:authored-additional-combat-phase | An additional combat phase has its own declare attackers step (CR 500.8, 506.1), and Relentless Assault untaps only creatures that attacked before it resolves: attack for 3, cast it in the second main phase to untap the Giant, and attack again for 3; cast before combat it untaps nothing, the Giant attacks in the extra combat and is still tapped for the regular one
